# EAS CLI compresses the project for build using .gitignore's patterns by
# default when no .easignore exists. This file overrides that for a LOCAL
# build's sake specifically (`eas build --local`) — cloud builds don't need
# any of these exclusions lifted, since they get GOOGLE_SERVICES_PLIST and
# every EXPO_PUBLIC_* env var injected separately via EAS's own cloud
# secrets, bypassing this archive entirely. A local build has no such
# injection step at all, so anything its prebuild or JS bundling step
# actually needs to read from disk has to be IN the archive, or the build
# either fails outright (missing GoogleService-Info.plist crashes prebuild)
# or silently succeeds with broken values baked in (a missing .env meant an
# earlier local build shipped with lib/supabase.ts's placeholder.supabase.co
# fallback silently baked into the bundle — verified via `strings` on the
# built .ipa, not caught by any build-time error).
#
# .env holds only EXPO_PUBLIC_* values here — meant to be public by Expo's
# own naming convention (they end up embedded in the shipped JS bundle
# regardless of how they got there), so there's no secrecy loss un-ignoring
# it. Confirmed: this repo's .env carries no non-EXPO_PUBLIC_ secrets; if
# that ever changes, split those into a separate git-ignored file instead of
# re-ignoring this one.

supabase/functions/.env
google-services.json

node_modules/

.expo/
dist/
web-build/

android/
ios/
!modules/*/ios/

.DS_Store
*.log
*.ipa
build-*.ipa
